# Line endings.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default), a checkout turns shell scripts
# into CRLF files, and a POSIX shell then fails with "bad interpreter: No such file
# or directory" because of the carriage return after the shebang. These entry points
# must work in bash/WSL/Git Bash and on Linux CI, so their line endings are pinned
# here rather than left to the developer's git config.
#
# Deliberately NOT a catch-all `* text=auto`: the already-committed YAML and
# dashboard JSON in this repository are CRLF in the working tree, and a global rule
# would renormalise them and show up as a large diff unrelated to any real change.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
